WEBVTT

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.860
The Crown Snowfield?!

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:09.490
The Crown Snowfield is a frigid area in Galar
with jagged, snowy mountains.

00:00:11.820 --> 00:00:13.160
It’s beautiful!

00:00:14.490 --> 00:00:19.170
And we’ve heard that someone there
“spotted a mysterious Pokémon.”

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.420
A mysterious Pokémon?!

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.540
What is it?!

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:25.960
That much,
we have yet to determine.

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.470
Which is why I’d like to have you start
by hearing from the man who saw it.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:31.550
Got it!

00:00:36.770 --> 00:00:38.480
Come with us, Koharu!

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.390
Come on!

00:00:42.110 --> 00:00:42.650
Sure!

00:00:42.650 --> 00:00:44.520
Okay then, Director...

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:46.150
<i>We’ll be off!</i>

00:00:46.150 --> 00:00:47.650
Be careful out there!

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:54.950
And so, Satoshi, Go, and Koharu make their way to
the Crown Snowfield, a place they have never been before.

00:00:56.240 --> 00:00:57.410
Meanwhile...

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:11.260
Lilie, a friend of Satoshi’s from Alola...

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:16.930
...searches for her missing father, Mohn,
along with her mother and brother.

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.570
...look after Lilie for me.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:37.450
Please protect...
my little princess.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:40.540
Father.

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.460
Snowball?

00:01:55.760 --> 00:01:58.350
The direction of that light...

00:01:58.350 --> 00:01:59.270
So it <i>is...</i>

00:01:59.270 --> 00:02:00.770
The Crown Snowfield!

00:02:00.770 --> 00:02:04.100
It lines up with what we got
from all the data we’ve gathered!

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.520
That’s where Father is...

00:03:51.920 --> 00:03:54.170
The mysterious Pokémon you saw...

00:03:54.170 --> 00:03:55.840
What shape was it?

00:03:56.220 --> 00:03:58.380
Mmmm...

00:03:58.380 --> 00:04:02.720
It was just this sudden “fwoosh,”
crossing my sight...

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.600
I couldn’t exactly say...

00:04:04.600 --> 00:04:06.520
And... its color?

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:07.480
What color was it?

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.230
Oh! Ohh!
Its color! It was white!

00:04:11.650 --> 00:04:13.360
So it was a white Pokémon.

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.360
Or was it?

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:16.860
“Or was it?”

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.900
No, yellow!

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.410
Yellow?!

00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:21.240
Or was it?

00:04:21.240 --> 00:04:22.700
“Or was it?”

00:04:22.700 --> 00:04:24.370
I know!
It was both!

00:04:24.370 --> 00:04:26.290
Both?

00:04:26.290 --> 00:04:28.620
<i>Or was it...?</i>

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:32.130
It was in the middle of a blizzard,
after all.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:35.050
Oh, there’s a blizzard today, too.

00:04:39.050 --> 00:04:40.300
When did it...?

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.010
It’s pure white!

00:04:42.010 --> 00:04:43.430
I can’t see a thing.

00:04:43.430 --> 00:04:44.890
See?

00:04:44.890 --> 00:04:50.560
Most people would’ve missed that Pokémon!
I only saw it ‘cause I’m used to blizzards.

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:53.310
Doubt it’s gonna clear up
anytime soon.

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.070
You should stay the night here.

00:04:57.110 --> 00:04:58.530
Are you sure?

00:04:58.530 --> 00:05:00.200
Of course!

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.410
<i>Thank you!</i>

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:08.830
The sun was shining until just a moment ago.
What is this?!

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.290
Are you all right?

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.250
Yes.

00:05:11.080 --> 00:05:12.250
Yeah!

00:05:16.130 --> 00:05:19.050
Ice types really are
impressively tough.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:28.350
Magearna?!

00:05:29.180 --> 00:05:29.680
Wait!

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.560
Zoroark!
Chase them with your Agility!

00:05:44.740 --> 00:05:47.120
Are you okay, Magearna?

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:50.370
Thank you, Zoroark.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:53.540
Let’s camp here for tonight.

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:55.420
Huh? Out in this blizzard?

00:05:56.040 --> 00:05:59.090
This is a new product developed by
the Aether Foundation!

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.770
I hope it’s sunny tomorrow.

00:06:10.770 --> 00:06:14.190
If it’s sunny, you’ll go looking
for the Pokémon the old man saw, right?

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.110
Not just looking.
We’re gonna catch it!

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:18.400
You bet!

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:20.150
I knew you’d say that.

00:06:44.970 --> 00:06:47.850
Father is...
just over there...

00:06:50.390 --> 00:06:51.220
Lilie!

00:06:59.610 --> 00:07:00.980
Please excuse me!

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:08.370
Is there nobody in?

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:33.930
Father!

00:07:33.930 --> 00:07:35.100
Huh?

00:07:36.480 --> 00:07:37.350
Um...

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.400
Who might you be?

00:07:42.110 --> 00:07:44.320
It’s me, Lilie.

00:07:44.320 --> 00:07:48.610
I expect you would only
know me as a baby,

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:50.530
but I am your daughter!

00:07:57.870 --> 00:07:59.380
Dad!

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.550
There, there...

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:06.760
Is this your Pokémon?

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:10.050
It’s Zoroark!

00:08:10.050 --> 00:08:12.220
Zoro... ark?

00:08:13.970 --> 00:08:16.680
Your old partner, Dad.

00:08:16.680 --> 00:08:18.520
Dad?

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:22.230
That’s right,
this girl was calling me that, too...

00:08:22.230 --> 00:08:24.110
What is all this about?

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:27.990
Mohn...

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:30.990
How do you know my name?

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:44.210
We’ve been searching
for my missing husband...

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:47.170
...the father of my children...

00:08:47.170 --> 00:08:49.760
We’ve traveled so far to get here.

00:08:50.220 --> 00:08:52.260
Missing?

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:57.520
We thought we’d finally see him again,
here in the Crown Snowfield...

00:08:57.520 --> 00:09:02.650
Oh, so that’s why your kids
mistook me for their father.

00:09:02.650 --> 00:09:03.770
I understand now.

00:09:07.530 --> 00:09:11.280
If you’d like,
you can come in for some tea.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:14.410
You must be tired
from your long trip.

00:09:19.210 --> 00:09:21.040
Thank you.

00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:23.750
We’ll accept your kind offer, then.

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:27.250
Please make yourselves at home.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:41.770
Mom.

00:09:41.770 --> 00:09:42.810
What do you think?

00:09:43.770 --> 00:09:46.650
If he doesn’t recognize us...

00:09:47.270 --> 00:09:49.610
He might have lost his memory.

00:09:49.610 --> 00:09:51.490
His memory...

00:09:51.490 --> 00:09:53.490
Thank you for waiting.

00:09:54.070 --> 00:09:55.830
Be careful, it’s hot.

00:09:57.080 --> 00:09:57.700
Here.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:09:59.450
Thank you.

00:09:59.450 --> 00:10:00.500
Here you go.

00:10:01.710 --> 00:10:04.750
I hope you like these.

00:10:09.340 --> 00:10:11.920
I need to introduce you
to my daughter.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.300
Your... daughter?!

00:10:15.640 --> 00:10:18.100
Still, what a coincidence.

00:10:18.100 --> 00:10:21.600
My daughter’s name is Lilie, too.

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:23.230
Lilie!

00:10:26.110 --> 00:10:27.400
I’ll go and call her.

00:10:28.690 --> 00:10:29.820
U-Um...

00:10:29.820 --> 00:10:30.320
Huh?

00:10:31.190 --> 00:10:33.400
May we come with you?

00:10:33.400 --> 00:10:34.280
Lilie?!

00:10:34.740 --> 00:10:36.490
Of course.

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:43.660
I’m coming in!

00:10:59.930 --> 00:11:01.770
Utsu... roid?!

00:11:08.730 --> 00:11:11.400
Stand back, Lilie, Gladio!

00:11:11.400 --> 00:11:13.740
We have visitors, Lilie.

00:11:18.780 --> 00:11:19.490
Zoroark!

00:11:21.450 --> 00:11:22.490
Let’s go!

00:11:22.490 --> 00:11:23.410
Wait!

00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:30.630
Huh? Lilie?

00:11:31.130 --> 00:11:34.970
I’m sorry.
My daughter’s quite shy.

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.430
Well, I’m sure
she’ll show herself at some point.

00:11:38.220 --> 00:11:41.010
Our teatime was interrupted.

00:11:41.010 --> 00:11:43.180
I’ll brew us some more.

00:11:46.980 --> 00:11:48.190
Why did you stop me?

00:11:48.190 --> 00:11:52.110
He thinks the Utsuroid
is his daughter.

00:11:52.110 --> 00:11:55.320
If you suddenly attacked it,
how do you think he’d react?

00:11:58.450 --> 00:12:01.330
There has to be
some reason for all of this.

00:12:01.700 --> 00:12:03.910
First, we need to find it out.

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:05.830
Let’s look for some clues.

00:12:07.540 --> 00:12:09.750
I’ll try talking with Mohn.

00:12:10.130 --> 00:12:12.800
If you see the Utsuroid,
tell me straight away.

00:12:13.420 --> 00:12:15.210
And be very careful.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:16.420
Right.

00:12:20.720 --> 00:12:22.850
Are we nearly there?

00:12:22.850 --> 00:12:25.560
We should be near the spot
where the old man saw the Pokémon!

00:12:26.140 --> 00:12:27.640
Or are we?

00:12:39.410 --> 00:12:40.280
What happened?

00:12:42.780 --> 00:12:44.370
They found something!

00:12:45.540 --> 00:12:46.620
Something?

00:13:12.900 --> 00:13:14.730
Lilie...

00:13:42.220 --> 00:13:43.430
The mirror...

00:13:50.560 --> 00:13:52.560
This one’s been removed, too...

00:14:22.260 --> 00:14:23.130
A mirror...

00:14:23.130 --> 00:14:25.640
Utsuroid hid it away.

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.230
Iron Tail!

00:14:37.400 --> 00:14:38.860
You okay, Lilie?!

00:14:40.150 --> 00:14:41.530
Satoshi!

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:42.530
What’s wrong?!

00:14:43.240 --> 00:14:44.400
Satoshi?!

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:45.570
Gladio?

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:46.620
Why are you here?

00:14:46.620 --> 00:14:51.750
When I went chasing after Pikachu,
I saw Utsuroid about to attack Lilie.

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:54.540
Pikachu!

00:14:54.540 --> 00:14:56.080
It’s been such a long time!

00:14:57.580 --> 00:14:59.090
Lilie?

00:14:59.090 --> 00:15:02.300
That girl who was traveling around
looking for her father?

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:03.470
Her father?

00:15:03.470 --> 00:15:06.840
Yes.
That is what led me here.

00:15:07.390 --> 00:15:10.010
Big Brother,
please look at this.

00:15:18.520 --> 00:15:19.860
This is my husband.

00:15:23.070 --> 00:15:25.150
This man...

00:15:25.150 --> 00:15:27.610
I don’t see
much of a resemblance.

00:15:28.370 --> 00:15:29.620
You really...

00:15:30.490 --> 00:15:33.200
You really can’t remember anything?

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:34.370
Mohn...

00:15:35.500 --> 00:15:36.750
Still...

00:15:38.710 --> 00:15:41.340
He looks very happy.

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:45.090
I hope you manage
to find him soon.

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:49.640
Mohn...

00:15:51.850 --> 00:15:53.220
The one that you...

00:15:53.890 --> 00:15:55.350
...called your daughter...

00:15:56.060 --> 00:15:58.230
...called Lilie, is...

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.480
Mom!

00:16:03.360 --> 00:16:05.650
Lilie, what are you doing?

00:16:08.990 --> 00:16:11.370
Wait, Utsuroid!

00:16:14.040 --> 00:16:15.370
Thank you.

00:16:15.870 --> 00:16:19.370
You rescued my father,
isn’t that right?

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:25.460
What... do you mean?

00:16:32.350 --> 00:16:34.260
Lilie, Gladio!

00:16:34.260 --> 00:16:35.270
We brought them.

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:43.610
We found this
in the piano room.

00:16:44.690 --> 00:16:45.860
What’s this?

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:50.030
I’m just guessing,
but I think the accident...

00:16:50.030 --> 00:16:52.700
...blasted you off
to some other world.

00:16:53.160 --> 00:16:54.490
Accident?

00:16:54.490 --> 00:16:56.200
What are you talking about?

00:16:56.700 --> 00:16:58.000
Mohn...

00:16:58.000 --> 00:17:01.460
You had an accident
while experimenting with Ultra Holes.

00:17:02.380 --> 00:17:03.210
Ultra...

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:06.800
...Holes.

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:13.300
In that world, you had some interaction with that Utsuroid,
and you returned to this world together.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:18.060
Except you didn’t return to the Alola Region,
but here, to the Crown Snowfield.

00:17:18.060 --> 00:17:22.190
And then,
you began living together in this house.

00:17:22.770 --> 00:17:24.480
As father and daughter.

00:17:52.050 --> 00:17:53.550
Lilie...

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:29.800
Lilie...

00:18:46.610 --> 00:18:48.190
Lilie...

00:18:48.900 --> 00:18:52.240
I don’t know why the Utsuroid
wanted to become Lilie.

00:18:52.740 --> 00:18:56.490
But you’ve lived
a happy life here, right?

00:18:57.120 --> 00:19:03.580
That’s why Utsuroid feared the possibility
of your memories returning if you saw your reflection.

00:19:04.250 --> 00:19:08.840
So it removed all of the mirrors
and made the windows dirty.

00:19:10.340 --> 00:19:12.210
If your memories returned...

00:19:13.010 --> 00:19:16.220
...it wouldn’t be able
to live with you anymore.

00:19:17.300 --> 00:19:20.560
When I saw that the mirror and clothes
had been carefully stored away...

00:19:21.310 --> 00:19:25.770
...I knew that you cherish my father.

00:19:25.770 --> 00:19:27.190
That’s what I realized.

00:19:27.560 --> 00:19:29.690
Even though you could have simply
thrown them away...

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:31.270
Dad.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:32.070
Hmm?

00:20:17.240 --> 00:20:20.280
I remember...
everything.

00:20:25.160 --> 00:20:26.120
Gladio.

00:20:26.120 --> 00:20:27.960
Dad!

00:20:27.960 --> 00:20:28.750
Lilie.

00:20:28.750 --> 00:20:30.290
Father!

00:20:33.300 --> 00:20:34.920
Lusamine.

00:20:36.260 --> 00:20:37.170
Mohn...

00:20:49.730 --> 00:20:52.560
Welcome back, Mohn!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.020
Welcome back!

00:20:52.560 --> 00:20:54.020
Welcome back, Dad!

00:20:54.940 --> 00:20:56.070
I’m home.

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:07.750
To think Magearna is working...

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:09.290
I can’t believe it.

00:21:09.290 --> 00:21:11.250
Lilie made it happen.

00:21:11.250 --> 00:21:13.840
My little princess did?

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.460
I could only do it
thanks to your Magearna journal.

00:21:25.100 --> 00:21:27.270
Stay, Lilie.

00:21:28.770 --> 00:21:31.480
I want that too, Lilie.

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:36.860
If not for you,
I’d never have reunited with my family.

00:21:38.070 --> 00:21:42.450
If you’d like to,
why don’t we keep on living together?

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:45.030
That’s a great idea, Mohn!

00:21:45.030 --> 00:21:46.450
I’m all for it, too.

00:21:50.370 --> 00:21:53.330
We’re both Lilie.
Isn’t that right?

00:22:05.640 --> 00:22:07.640
Let’s go home, together.

00:22:22.610 --> 00:22:29.080
And so, Mohn, Lusamine,
Gladio, and Lilie’s family...

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:35.210
...became united once again,
and they set off into a brand new future.

00:24:02.170 --> 00:24:04.590
Now! Onto the next adventure!

00:24:04.590 --> 00:24:05.880
Go!

00:24:06.590 --> 00:24:08.220
A Battle Royal?!

00:24:08.220 --> 00:24:09.590
What’s a Battle Royal?

00:24:09.590 --> 00:24:13.310
It’s this awesome type of
Pokémon battle they do in Alola!

00:24:13.310 --> 00:24:15.230
“Awesome”? Awesome how?

00:24:15.230 --> 00:24:16.310
They have this ring,

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:24.570
and they go “wham, boom, bam-bam-bam-bam-bam,”
and then “grrrr, fwoosh, mrraaaaggh, hiy—”

00:24:24.570 --> 00:24:26.650
Next time, on Pocket Monsters:

00:24:26.650 --> 00:24:29.160
A Triumphant Return!
The Champion of Alola!!
